    "descripcion": "Entender las ideas principales de textos complejos de su campo de especialización. Relacionarse con hablantes nativos con cierto grado de fluidez y naturalidad.Producir textos claros y detallados sobre temas diversos. Defender su punto de vista sobre temas generales. Al finalizar el curso el estudiante presenta el (PET) Preliminary English Test que corresponde al nivel intermedio B1 del CEFR. Conceptos Previos No requiere conceptos previos.",
    "contenido": "Talking about eating habits, telling a story, talking about sports, families,Present simple & continuous,Action & non-action verbs, Past simple, continuous & perfect, Future, going to Understanding a news program, money & currency, talking about road safety, present perfect, simple past, present perfect continuous, comparatives, superlatives Describing people, talking about manners, talking about cell phones, matching people with their jobs, talking about abilities,must, have to, should (obligation), must, may, might, can't (deduction), can, could, be able to (ability and possibility. Talking about education, describing dreams & desires, talking about friendship,things you used to do,have,etc. First conditional, future time clauses+when,until, etc. Second conditional, usually & used to Planning a new city, men vs. Women, talking about work, imaging doing other jobs, quantifiers, articles:a/an, the, no article, verbs and adjectives + preposition, connectors:however, according to, on the other hand, also, while, gerunds & infinitives. Complaining, going shopping, talking about movies, interviewing famous people: heroes and icons of our time, describing a person you admire, understanding a radio program, reported speech:statements, questions and commands, passive (be + past participle), relative clauses: defining and non-defining. Talking about objects people couldn't live without, making conclusions, talking about tv habits, interviewing, third conditional, tag questions, indirect questions, phrasal verbs , compound nouns, making adjectives and adverbs. BIBLIOGRAFÍA [1] Oxeden Clive, Christina Latham-Koening. American English File 3. Oxford University Press- UK New York 2008 [2] Summers Della, Adrian-Vallance E. et al. Active Study Dictionary New Edition. Longman- Edinburgh 2004 [3] Leech Geoffrey & Jan Svartvik. A Communicative Grammar of English. Longman- London 1975 [4] A Godman/EMF Payne. Dictionary of Scientific Usage. Longman Group Ltd.- Harlow & London 1979"
